{"content":[{"c":["GATH-RIMMON"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. City located in the land allotted to Dan’s tribe for an inheritance (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.19.45","r":"Josh.19.45","rawR":"Josh.19.45","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.19.45","value":"Josh.19.45"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 19:45"},"). It was assigned as one of the four Levitical cities for the Kohathites in Dan (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.21.24","r":"Josh.21.24","rawR":"Josh.21.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.21.24","value":"Josh.21.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:24"},"). Lost to the Canaanites, Gath-rimmon was later regained by Ephraim and included as one of its cities for the sons of Levi (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.69","r":"1Chr.6.69","rawR":"1Chr.6.69","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.69","value":"1Chr.6.69"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:69"},"). Its site is identifiable with the modern Tell el-Jerisheh."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=LeviticalCities_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"LeviticalCities_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"LeviticalCities_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Levitical Cities"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["2. One of two cities given to the Levites in Manasseh west of the Jordan River (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.21.25","r":"Josh.21.25","rawR":"Josh.21.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.21.25","value":"Josh.21.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 21:25"},"), suggesting a possible transcription mistake, which is better read as Bileam (cf. ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.70","r":"1Chr.6.70","rawR":"1Chr.6.70","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.70","value":"1Chr.6.70"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:70"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"GathRimmon","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 19:45","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.19.45","rawQueryValue":"Josh.19.45","sourceRefExact":"Josh.19.45"},{"anchorText":"21:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.21.24","rawQueryValue":"Josh.21.24","sourceRefExact":"Josh.21.24"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:69","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.69","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.69","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.69"},{"anchorText":"Jos 21:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.21.25","rawQueryValue":"Josh.21.25","sourceRefExact":"Josh.21.25"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:70","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.70","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.70","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.70"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"f4aaf9d57dc0ec83511b5c578aa2077a3f55f8a5c1582c0d5b7af1df559f5fff","sourceItemName":"GathRimmon","sourceItemOrder":54,"sourceMember":"Articles/G.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"GathRimmon","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Gath-Rimmon","title":"Gath-Rimmon","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}